{"t":1369608.9469872,"req":"q12","event":"done","status":"answered","level":0,"steps":["classify","retrieve","tool","draft"],"answer":"The routing module measures the similarity between adjacent encoder outputs: it projects each output into query q\u209c and key k\u209c vectors, computes the cosine similarity between q\u209c and k\u209c\u208b\u2081, rescales it to a boundary probability p\u209c = \u00bd(1 \u2212 cosine), and then places a boundary whenever p\u209c \u2265 0.5 (with p\u2081 = 1.0 by definition)[C:dynchunk:20]. This similarity\u2011based scoring is the core mechanism for predicting chunk boundaries[C:dynchunk:7]."}
